msgid "Agent overview"
msgstr "Vue d’ensemble des agents"

#. Settings page and Ctrl+K, a setting's name, the row label (a choice that opens a list). What it does: How large agents' portraits are in the explorer; opens a list of sizes.
#. Settings page and Ctrl+K, a preference's name, the row label. What it does: Size of the agents' portraits in the explorer, compact rows and cards
msgid "Agent picture size"
msgstr "Taille des images des agents"

#. chat pane border, accessibility label of the agent's name in the top right corner (a button that opens the agent's profile)
#. chat header, accessibility label of the agent's name, which opens the agent's profile (noun)
#. Ctrl+K command palette, a command's name (an action; a verb phrase is a command, a noun phrase names what it opens). What it does: Opens the open agent's profile: its artifacts and images, files, terminal, voice, plan, prompt history, model and backend.
#. Keys (key context “Everywhere”): the name of a key's action, in the shortcut bar, Keys help (?) and the key-binding editor. It opens the open agent's profile: its artifacts and images, files, terminal, voice, plan, prompt history, model and backend.
#. Key-binding editor and Keys help, the name of a key context (where a key works): an agent's profile
#. Vim mode, the which-key panel: what the keys "<Space> p" do in the chat and the explorer
msgid "Agent profile"
msgstr "Profil de l’agent"

#. quick switcher (Ctrl+K), placeholder of the search field: what can be found by typing
#. Ctrl+K command palette, placeholder of the search field: what it finds
msgid "Agent, contact, setting or command"
msgstr "Agent, contact, paramètre ou commande"

#. composer, accessibility label of the list of agents that pop up while typing @ (to mention one)
msgid "Agents to mention"
msgstr "Agents à mentionner"

